+# Epic Story Breakdown: Capture and review
+
+**Epic**: E001 - Capture and review  
+**Project**: 001-pulseboard  
+**Created**: 2026-08-10  
+**Version**: 1.0  
+**Status**: Draft
+
+---
+
+## Information Sources
+
+**Traceability**: This breakdown was created from:
+
+- `epic.md` — user outcome and protected boundaries.
+- `epic-tech-spec.md` — workspace-scoped storage, asynchronous extraction, review loading scope, and confirmation invariant.
+- `traceability-matrix.md` — three promise rows mapped below.
+- No PRD, constitution, codebase scan, or project constraints artifact is present in the supplied workspace.
+
+## Summary
+
+**Total Stories**: 3  
+**Epic Dependencies**: None evidenced  
+**Estimated Duration**: To be estimated during story planning  
+**Parallelization Potential**: Low — the workspace boundary is prerequisite to the capture and review flows.
+
+## Story Organization
+
+### Phase 1: Foundation setup
+
+- [ ] S001 Workspace-scoped capture and action records
+  - **Type**: Technical / security boundary
+  - **Details**: Scope transcript and proposed-action persistence and active-workspace reads to `workspace_id`.
+  - **References**: `epic-tech-spec.md` — workspace storage and review UI scope
+  - **Duration**: To be estimated during story planning
+
+### Phase 2: Core capture
+
+- [ ] S002 Transcript capture and asynchronous action extraction
+  - **Type**: Core user story
+  - **Story**: As a facilitator, I want to upload a transcript and receive proposed action items so that I can begin a review.
+  - **Depends on**: S001
+  - **References**: `epic.md`; `epic-tech-spec.md` — asynchronous extraction
+  - **Duration**: To be estimated during story planning
+
+### Phase 3: Review and confirmation
+
+- [ ] S003 Review, edit, and explicit confirmation of proposed actions
+  - **Type**: Core user story
+  - **Story**: As a facilitator, I want to edit and explicitly confirm proposed actions so that confirmed commitments are deliberate and complete.
+  - **Depends on**: S001, S002
+  - **References**: `epic.md`; `epic-tech-spec.md` — active workspace review and confirmation requirements
+  - **Duration**: To be estimated during story planning
+
+### Phase 4: Quality and polish
+
+No separate quality-only story is justified by the supplied evidence. Workspace isolation, asynchronous extraction behavior, and the explicit-confirmation invariant are acceptance boundaries of S001–S003 and will be specified and verified within those stories.
+
+## Story Details
+
+### S001: Workspace-scoped capture and action records
+
+**Acceptance boundary**: transcripts and proposed actions are stored and retrieved only for the active workspace.  
+**Technical implementation (high level)**: establish `workspace_id` ownership for transcript and action records; require active-workspace scope on review reads.  
+**Traceability**: PRM-004 → S001 / AC-1.
+
+### S002: Transcript capture and asynchronous action extraction
+
+**Acceptance boundary**: a facilitator can upload a transcript and the system produces proposed actions asynchronously within that workspace.  
+**Technical implementation (high level)**: persist the upload under the workspace boundary and invoke asynchronous extraction.  
+**Traceability**: PRM-001 → S002 / AC-1.
+
+### S003: Review, edit, and explicit confirmation of proposed actions
+
+**Acceptance boundary**: a facilitator can edit a proposed action; confirmation requires text, owner, and a future due date, and records confirmer and timestamp without implicit confirmation.  
+**Technical implementation (high level)**: load only the active workspace's proposals; validate the confirmation invariant and persist confirmation attribution.  
+**Traceability**: PRM-002 → S003 / AC-1.
+
+## Execution Strategy
+
+### Parallel Execution Groups
+
+No parallel implementation group is safe from the supplied technical constraints. S001 establishes the mandatory workspace boundary; S002 depends on it; S003 depends on both the boundary and extracted proposals.
+
+### Critical Path
+
+S001 → S002 → S003 → Complete
+
+## Dependencies
+
+### External Dependencies
+
+- No external service, library, or epic dependency is evidenced in the supplied planning corpus.
+
+### Inter-Story Dependencies
+
+| Story | Depends On | Provides To |
+|------|------------|-------------|
+| S001 | — | S002, S003 |
+| S002 | S001 | S003 |
+| S003 | S001, S002 | — |
+
+## Risk Mitigation
+
+| Story | Risk | Mitigation |
+|------|------|------------|
+| S001 | Cross-workspace data exposure | Make active-workspace scope an acceptance boundary before capture or review work proceeds. |
+| S002 | Extraction appears complete before the asynchronous work finishes | Specify observable asynchronous states during `/story-specify`. |
+| S003 | An action is confirmed implicitly or with incomplete commitment data | Specify and verify the required text, owner, future due date, confirmer, and timestamp. |
+
+## Definition of Done
+
+Per story completion is deferred to `/story-specify`, `/story-plan`, `/story-tasks`, implementation, audit, and validation. This breakdown has only created Draft (Placeholder) specs and mapped the epic promises.
+
+## Next Steps
+
+1. Run `/story-specify` on S001, then S002, then S003.
+2. Run `/epic-analyze` to validate this breakdown before implementation if required by the epic flow.
+
